Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dsi: power off the bonded slave before its clock master

A same-mode OFF/ON cycle on SM8750 Piano a8c9650e reports DSI1 pixel,
byte-interface and byte branch clocks stuck on. The captured return address
is the second power_off in dsi_mgr_bridge_post_disable(), after host0 has
already stopped its link clocks. DSI1 sources its clocks from DSI0's PHY PLL.

Qualcomm's fixed public clock manager disables non-master link and core
clocks before the clock master. Match that sequence in the normal bonded
shutdown, as the existing power_off error unwind already does. Leave PLL
save/restore, the final dual-PHY disable, panel timing and halt checking intact.

Source: MiCode/vendor_opensource_display-drivers aa06fd1757c28dce96fbe4e04d4530ec21b52aac
msm/dsi/dsi_clk_manager.c:705-794

This candidate is not enabled or hardware tested. It addresses the actual
shutdown order difference, not initial-probe PLL warnings, and does not claim
60Hz modeset or system suspend recovery until the same-mode cycle is tested.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_manager.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_manager.c
@@ -367,16 +367,20 @@
 	/* Save PHY status if it is a clock source */
 	msm_dsi_phy_pll_save_state(msm_dsi->phy);
 
-	ret = msm_dsi_host_power_off(host);
-	if (ret)
-		pr_err("%s: host %d power off failed,%d\n", __func__, id, ret);
-
+	/* Keep the clock-source host running until the bonded slave's link
+	 * clocks have stopped. Match the reverse power-on order and the
+	 * existing dsi_mgr_bridge_power_off() unwind path.
+	 */
 	if (is_bonded_dsi && msm_dsi1) {
 		ret = msm_dsi_host_power_off(msm_dsi1->host);
 		if (ret)
 			pr_err("%s: host1 power off failed, %d\n",
 								__func__, ret);
 	}
+
+	ret = msm_dsi_host_power_off(host);
+	if (ret)
+		pr_err("%s: host %d power off failed,%d\n", __func__, id, ret);
 
 disable_phy:
 	dsi_mgr_phy_disable(id);
